{
  "$comment": "#EXP-1841 (Danny 2026-11-14: 'the composer inside a chat should behave like the new-message composer when an image is attached', one composer, the exact same logic): THE attachment strip of EVERY composer x4 — a new chat's (the launch composer, 'To <agent>'), a session's, an agent chat's, the Assistant's, an app editor's — and its positional `[Image #N]` placeholders (EXP-698): web `lib/pending-images.ts` (both `hooks/use-launch-composer.ts` and `components/session-composer.tsx`), desktop `domain::composer_attachments` (ui `composer_images`), iOS ExpCore `ComposerAttachments.swift`, Android `domain/ComposerAttachments.kt`; model = pure `src/composer-attachments.ts`, every mirror replays ALL four case lists and compares the WHOLE expected value. The strip is a list of kinds in order; classifying a picked file stays the platform's (an accepted image type up to 10 MB = `image`, any other file up to 50 MB = `file`, empty or over its cap = `rejected`). ATTACH (picker, paste, drag-and-drop, the share sheet; one pick may carry several files): `stage` takes them in pick order; each TAKEN image drops its marker at the caret (`insert`: a space before it unless the caret is at the start or after whitespace, a space after it unless the caret is at the end or before whitespace) and the caret moves behind it, so several images read `[Image #1] [Image #2]`; numbering continues from the images ALREADY in the strip (image #1 = the strip's first IMAGE; files carry no marker and never count). Images and files each cap at FOUR; a pick over a cap or refused stays out and the composer shows `toasts` (in that order) as its error toast. REMOVE (the thumbnail's X): `drop` removes the entry; an image's markers leave the draft (every occurrence; only lines that LOST a marker are tidied: doubled spaces collapse, trailing ones go, and a line that started with it loses its lead space) and every higher marker slides down one (`renumber`), so the numbers keep matching the strip. A file's X leaves the text alone. A marker the user deleted or typed by hand is just text. SEND: the text goes as typed (markers included, plain text on the wire) with the attachment ids in strip order; the server writes the image embeds and file links (steer-image-message). Nothing else differs between the composers.",
  "insert": [
    {
      "name": "an empty draft holds the marker alone",
      "input": {
        "text": "",
